Seed: CompareTo with a null range is rewritten only when compared with 0 and only for a null operand, as #227 shipped it
Oracles: RangeOrderParityTests
Fails: CompareTo(null) == 1, >= 1, > -1, != -1 and 1 == CompareTo(null) (no rows, memory every row), and a NULL column, which Comparer<T>.Default orders equal to null and before every range
History: found by the final pre-release analysis (#256, #261) before 10.0.0 shipped

